reg_decoder_fld_t tof3_dprsr_hi_regs__dprsr_hi_regs_h__h__max_src_chunks_fld_list[] = {
    { "cfg", 4, 0, 0,0, 
      "The new header can reference segments (aka CLOTs) of data from the original packet. The source packet is treated as chunks of 16B. Thsi register specifies the offset of the last chunk that must be read. For example, the last byte that might be referenced by a segment could be 15. i.e. no CLOTS in the current P4  reference any bytes beyond byte 15 of an incoming packet. Byte 15 is in the first 16B chunk, so this register would be set to 1. If the last byte referenced was byte 383 (the maximum the hardware supports) then this is in the 24th chunk (24*16 = 384) so this register would be set to 24 (the default). Setting this to the smallest number used by the P4 program can result in optimum (lowest) latency." },
};
