reg_decoder_fld_t tof3_dprsr_out_ingr__cfg48_mask_fld_list[] = {
    { "cfg", 19, 0, 0,0, 
      "Specify the cfg_mask used to match against the live data.  Counter ctr will increment when the expression   ( live_data & cfg_mask[ctr] ) == cfg_data[ctr]    evaluates to true. Live data is logic evaluated by the ingress and egress decision blocks. There are two sources of live data. The data_sel register must be set to specify the live data source for each counter.  Source 0 (data_sel bit is 0) is from the Arbitration and Control logic: [19] ctr_arb_rd_data.mirrhdr_pop,  1 = Mirror Hdr (0-48bytes) is popped. [18] ctr_arb_rd_data.mirrmeta_pop, 1 = Mirror metadata is popped. [17] ctr_arb_rd_data.new_cell_vld,  1 =  a Main cell is created. [16] ctr_arb_rd_data.pktdata_pop, 1 = Packet data is popped (1-11 16B chunks). [15] ctr_arb_rd_data.pktdata_rd,  1 = Packet data is being read. [14] ctr_arb_rd_data.pkthdr_pop, 1 = A packet hdr cell is being popped. [13] ctr_arb_rd_data.mainmeta_read,  1 = Main pkt metadata is being read. [12] ctr_arb_rd_data.mainmeta_pop, 1 = Main pkt metadata is popped (finished). [11] ctr_arb_rd_data.mirr,  1 = This cell is mirrored. [10] ctr_arb_rd_data.eop, 1 = This cell is EOP. [9] ctr_arb_rd_data.sop, 1 = This cell is SOP. [8] ctr_arb_mac2, 1 if any channel from MAC2. [7] ctr_arb_mac1, 1 if any channel from MAC1. [6] ctr_arb_mac0, 1 if any channel from MAC0. [5:1] ctr_arb_chan, (channel 0-17 0-7=MAC1 8-15=MAC2 16-17=MAC0). [0] ctr_arb_vld   (1 = ctr_arb data is valid. An arbiter word has been read from the FIFO.) Source 1 (data_sel bit is 1) is from the incoming xPB module (incoming data): [18] ctr_xpb_err_2,  1 = This MAC 2 channel encountered an error (also select EOP)  [17] ctr_xpb_eop_2,  1 = This MAC 2 channel word is EOP  [16] ctr_xpb_sop_2,  1 = This MAC 2 channel word is SOP  [15:13] ctr_xpb_chn_2, Identifies the channel 0-7 within MAC 2.  [12] ctr_xpb_vld_2,  1 = MAC2 information is valid.  [11] ctr_xpb_err_1,  Same for MAC 1 [10] ctr_xpb_eop_1,  [9] ctr_xpb_sop_1,  [8:6] ctr_xpb_chn_1, [5] ctr_xpb_vld_1,  [4] ctr_xpb_err_0, Same for MAC 0  [3] ctr_xpb_eop_0,  [2] ctr_xpb_sop_0,  [1] ctr_xpb_chn_0,  Identifies the channel 0-1 within MAC 0.  [0] ctr_xpb_vld_0, " },
};
